1
00:00:13,247 --> 00:00:14,682
[Negan] Previously
on Dead City...

2
00:00:14,782 --> 00:00:16,650
For a wanted man,
I look good!

3
00:00:16,750 --> 00:00:18,152
[Armstrong] I'm a
New Babylon marshal.

4
00:00:18,252 --> 00:00:19,653
Have you seen this man?

5
00:00:19,753 --> 00:00:21,189
Manhattan was one
of the epicenters.

6
00:00:21,289 --> 00:00:22,756
Military destroyed all
the bridges and tunnels

7
00:00:22,856 --> 00:00:24,024
hoping to contain it.

8
00:00:24,125 --> 00:00:25,593
[Amaia] What are you after?

9
00:00:25,693 --> 00:00:26,794
It's pretty obvious

10
00:00:26,894 --> 00:00:27,828
you dickheads
ain't from around here.

11
00:00:27,928 --> 00:00:29,530
The Croat, he has my son.

12
00:00:29,630 --> 00:00:31,031
[Amaia] So you wanna
get to the psycho.

13
00:00:31,132 --> 00:00:32,600
That, we can help you with.

14
00:00:32,700 --> 00:00:35,703
[Negan] He was an exceptionally
insane son of a bitch.

15
00:00:35,803 --> 00:00:37,105
I'll put up that girl.

16
00:00:37,205 --> 00:00:39,840
Ginny, I will come
back for you soon.

17
00:00:39,940 --> 00:00:40,974
[crickets chirping]

18
00:00:43,577 --> 00:00:47,981
[birds chirping]

19
00:00:54,054 --> 00:00:57,591
[walker growling]

20
00:01:03,297 --> 00:01:05,166
[grunts]

21
00:01:08,336 --> 00:01:11,004
We gotta talk.
Scratch that,

22
00:01:11,105 --> 00:01:13,039
you gotta talk.

23
00:01:13,141 --> 00:01:14,542
You need help?

24
00:01:14,642 --> 00:01:17,478
How am I supposed to know
if you ain't yelling for it?

25
00:01:17,578 --> 00:01:20,013
All I have been doing for months

26
00:01:20,114 --> 00:01:22,383
is trying to find
a safe place for you,

27
00:01:22,483 --> 00:01:25,553
and you have been sticking
to me like goddamn crazy glue.

28
00:01:25,652 --> 00:01:27,388
I turn my back
for half a second,

29
00:01:27,488 --> 00:01:29,723
and that's when
you decide to skedaddle!?

30
00:01:29,823 --> 00:01:32,960
[birds chirping]

31
00:01:42,303 --> 00:01:43,871
Yeah.

32
00:01:43,971 --> 00:01:46,907
This asswipe tried
to kill us last night.

33
00:01:47,007 --> 00:01:49,443
Guess we ain't the
only ones he pissed off.

34
00:01:53,614 --> 00:01:54,682
Can you at least tell me

35
00:01:54,782 --> 00:01:56,584
what the hell
you're doin' out here?

36
00:01:56,684 --> 00:02:00,154
[birds chirping]

37
00:02:05,893 --> 00:02:09,263
[Negan] You lost your dino.
Goddamn it.

38
00:02:09,363 --> 00:02:11,332
Dropped it, huh?

39
00:02:14,668 --> 00:02:17,605
Okay. All right.

40
00:02:17,704 --> 00:02:21,841
We will just re-goddamn-trace
our goddamn footsteps.

41
00:02:22,710 --> 00:02:28,749
[loud, clunky engine running]

42
00:02:32,152 --> 00:02:34,021
[engine stops running]

43
00:02:34,888 --> 00:02:36,824
[seagulls squawking]
[waves lapping]

44
00:02:36,924 --> 00:02:43,030
[unsettling music]

45
00:02:56,744 --> 00:03:02,716
[music intensifies]

46
00:03:08,889 --> 00:03:14,962
[theme music]

47
00:03:58,472 --> 00:04:03,176
[clacking]

48
00:04:11,151 --> 00:04:12,986
[seagulls squawking]

49
00:04:13,086 --> 00:04:17,858
[clacking continues]

50
00:04:30,504 --> 00:04:32,540
[dings bell]

51
00:04:33,841 --> 00:04:36,744
[Negan laughs]
What do you got there?

52
00:04:36,844 --> 00:04:38,579
It's beeswax.

53
00:04:38,679 --> 00:04:40,648
I hear that's good for cuts.
Can I bum a little bit?

54
00:04:41,715 --> 00:04:43,183
No.

55
00:04:43,683 --> 00:04:45,753
[Amaia] Eighth is safe
until around 30th,

56
00:04:45,853 --> 00:04:47,120
then we'll loop around.

57
00:04:47,220 --> 00:04:48,789
[Tommaso] Might as well
be a map of the moon.

58
00:04:48,889 --> 00:04:50,524
Or Yonkers.

59
00:04:50,624 --> 00:04:52,760
Most of these streets are no-go,

60
00:04:52,860 --> 00:04:54,595
jammed wall-to-wall
with fleshies.

61
00:04:54,695 --> 00:04:56,096
What about 33rd?

62
00:04:56,196 --> 00:04:58,766
[Amaia] Nah, he's got traps
all up and down the 30's.

63
00:04:58,866 --> 00:05:00,834
How long you
guys been at this?

64
00:05:02,302 --> 00:05:05,773
We ain't tourists,
that's for sure.

65
00:05:05,873 --> 00:05:08,642
Just... kids
when it all went down.

66
00:05:11,044 --> 00:05:13,447
The first few weeks
were the worst.

67
00:05:13,547 --> 00:05:15,483
I mean, it spread so fast.

68
00:05:15,583 --> 00:05:18,251
Through the subways,
the buildings.

69
00:05:18,352 --> 00:05:20,421
Bodies coming up
from the ground,

70
00:05:20,521 --> 00:05:22,456
falling from the sky.

71
00:05:22,556 --> 00:05:24,625
[sighs]

72
00:05:24,725 --> 00:05:26,594
We kept waiting for
the Army to show up.

73
00:05:26,694 --> 00:05:29,763
Shit, anybody.

74
00:05:29,863 --> 00:05:32,232
And when they finally got here,

75
00:05:32,332 --> 00:05:36,604
we were dumb enough to think
that they'd come to save us.

76
00:05:36,704 --> 00:05:39,272
Then we watched them
blow up the bridges,

77
00:05:39,373 --> 00:05:41,074
the tunnels.

78
00:05:41,174 --> 00:05:43,644
Leaving us in this death trap.

79
00:05:43,744 --> 00:05:47,180
We were getting it together
little by little,

80
00:05:47,280 --> 00:05:50,451
till he showed up.
Asking people to join him,

81
00:05:50,551 --> 00:05:54,455
offering protection,
creature comforts.

82
00:05:54,555 --> 00:05:56,323
What's he want with you?

83
00:05:56,424 --> 00:05:57,691
To keep us safe.

84
00:05:57,791 --> 00:06:00,027
His paranoid,
crazy version of that.

85
00:06:00,127 --> 00:06:01,762
Kill or be killed.

86
00:06:01,862 --> 00:06:03,631
[Amaia] We were never
gonna sign up for that.

87
00:06:03,731 --> 00:06:06,500
We don't take no orders from
no bridge-and-tunnel nutcase.

88
00:06:06,600 --> 00:06:09,837
[Tommaso] So now
he tries to kill us.

89
00:06:09,937 --> 00:06:11,038
Steal from us.

90
00:06:11,138 --> 00:06:12,372
Catch and torture us,

91
00:06:12,473 --> 00:06:15,543
so he can learn how to
kill and steal some more.

92
00:06:15,643 --> 00:06:19,046
Only one of us
ever got out alive,

93
00:06:19,146 --> 00:06:21,549
and that wasn't
anything but luck.

94
00:06:21,649 --> 00:06:23,584
I've gotta go check the alley.

95
00:06:26,787 --> 00:06:28,522
Oh, shit.

96
00:06:28,622 --> 00:06:29,690
I'm sorry, I didn't mean to--

97
00:06:29,790 --> 00:06:31,792
No, it's all right.

98
00:06:31,892 --> 00:06:33,226
She's tougher than she looks,

99
00:06:33,326 --> 00:06:35,763
and she looks tough as shit.

100
00:06:37,465 --> 00:06:43,571
[tries to breathe down sobs]

101
00:06:47,641 --> 00:06:52,012
[creaking]
[waves lapping]

102
00:06:58,185 --> 00:07:04,291
[tense music]

103
00:07:05,358 --> 00:07:08,295
[seagulls squawking]

104
00:07:23,644 --> 00:07:27,548
[loud whirring]
[walkers growling]

105
00:07:27,648 --> 00:07:29,382
[Tommaso] Wanna
get to the Croat,

106
00:07:29,483 --> 00:07:30,918
we just gotta get through that.

107
00:07:31,018 --> 00:07:33,954
It's been bringing fleshies in
from all over the city.

108
00:07:34,054 --> 00:07:35,789
[Amaia] Right on cue.

109
00:07:35,889 --> 00:07:41,729
[music playing from float]
[walkers growling]

110
00:07:46,199 --> 00:07:48,435
God dang, the parade's lookin'
a little rough this year.

111
00:07:48,536 --> 00:07:49,703
[Maggie] How do we
get inside the arena?

112
00:07:49,803 --> 00:07:52,606
You don't.

113
00:07:52,706 --> 00:07:54,107
-Sewers.
-[Amaia] Hell no.

114
00:07:54,207 --> 00:07:56,409
Army shoved in all
the fleshies they killed

115
00:07:56,510 --> 00:07:58,779
till they got turned
into fleshies too.

116
00:07:58,879 --> 00:08:00,614
Sealed it up nice and tight.

117
00:08:00,714 --> 00:08:03,283
[Negan] You said one
of your people got out.

118
00:08:03,383 --> 00:08:06,954
Look, I'm just extrapolating
here, but...

119
00:08:07,054 --> 00:08:08,622
if someone broke
out of Alcatraz--

120
00:08:08,722 --> 00:08:12,760
Then there's a way back in.
Who escaped?

121
00:08:14,595 --> 00:08:19,299
Tommaso, just tell us
how you got out.

122
00:08:19,399 --> 00:08:21,301
It's all we need to know.

123
00:08:21,401 --> 00:08:24,337
Or... we could show them.

124
00:08:24,437 --> 00:08:26,640
No. The decision's
already been made.

125
00:08:26,740 --> 00:08:28,141
So, what, we're just
gonna sit around,

126
00:08:28,241 --> 00:08:29,476
twiddling our dicks?

127
00:08:29,577 --> 00:08:31,779
He invaded our home!
He butchered our people!

128
00:08:31,879 --> 00:08:33,145
-We can't just--
-Luther's right.

129
00:08:33,246 --> 00:08:35,148
It was a risk when we voted it
down the first time.

130
00:08:35,248 --> 00:08:37,684
And now there's even
less of us, and I...

131
00:08:37,784 --> 00:08:40,320
I don't know if I can...

132
00:08:40,419 --> 00:08:42,690
I mean...

133
00:08:42,789 --> 00:08:44,958
Going back there is, like...

134
00:08:45,058 --> 00:08:48,629
I am, um, getting a
little feeling of déjà vu.

135
00:08:49,797 --> 00:08:52,766
Twelve, fifteen years ago,
there was a...

136
00:08:52,866 --> 00:08:54,868
a fella down south.

137
00:08:54,968 --> 00:08:58,839
Showed up out of nowhere,
a lot like this guy.

138
00:08:58,939 --> 00:09:01,975
Everybody flocked to him because
he knew what they needed,

139
00:09:02,075 --> 00:09:06,279
what they wanted.
Protection.

140
00:09:06,379 --> 00:09:07,948
Sanctuary.

141
00:09:08,048 --> 00:09:10,517
So we built a badass fortress.

142
00:09:10,618 --> 00:09:13,954
Formed an army out of
psychopaths.

143
00:09:14,054 --> 00:09:15,956
And he forced people to join.

144
00:09:16,056 --> 00:09:17,658
And if they didn't?

145
00:09:17,758 --> 00:09:20,193
The hammer came down.

146
00:09:20,293 --> 00:09:23,163
Now soon enough, the people,
they got fed up with it,

147
00:09:23,263 --> 00:09:24,865
so they got together.

148
00:09:24,965 --> 00:09:29,202
And they decided it was time
to take that hammer back.

149
00:09:29,302 --> 00:09:32,806
-So what happened?
-It worked.

150
00:09:32,906 --> 00:09:34,842
Hell yeah it worked.

151
00:09:34,942 --> 00:09:38,111
[whirring in background]

152
00:09:42,315 --> 00:09:43,116
[sighs]

153
00:09:45,018 --> 00:09:48,922
We'll talk to the others.

154
00:09:50,323 --> 00:09:53,627
[tires screeching]

155
00:09:55,362 --> 00:10:03,637
[tense music]

156
00:10:33,466 --> 00:10:35,402
Welcome!

157
00:10:37,204 --> 00:10:43,310
[music grows darker]

158
00:11:01,428 --> 00:11:07,200
[indistinct chatter in distance]

159
00:11:08,736 --> 00:11:09,970
[Tommaso] Sometimes
the door would open

160
00:11:10,070 --> 00:11:13,340
and he'd offer me
food or medicine.

161
00:11:13,440 --> 00:11:16,076
All I had to do
was start talking.

162
00:11:16,176 --> 00:11:19,146
How many of us were left,
where we were hiding.

163
00:11:19,246 --> 00:11:20,613
[chuckles]

164
00:11:20,714 --> 00:11:23,583
But I knew the second
I talked, I'd be axed, so...

165
00:11:23,683 --> 00:11:27,154
you know, the door kept opening.

166
00:11:27,254 --> 00:11:29,723
But let's just say there was
no more food and medicine.

167
00:11:31,091 --> 00:11:32,960
When I was a kid,

168
00:11:33,060 --> 00:11:34,828
my nonno used to talk
about working on the crew

169
00:11:34,928 --> 00:11:36,496
that rebuilt Penn Station.

170
00:11:36,596 --> 00:11:39,165
People assumed the
old station was gone.

171
00:11:39,266 --> 00:11:42,803
But Gramps, he knew the spots
where they left the framework

172
00:11:42,903 --> 00:11:45,973
hiding behind the walls.

173
00:11:46,073 --> 00:11:47,374
So one night, the Burazi

174
00:11:47,474 --> 00:11:49,977
were kind enough
to clean out my cell

175
00:11:50,077 --> 00:11:52,012
from all the blood
they spilt in there.

176
00:11:52,112 --> 00:11:55,182
And lucky for me,
a fleshie got in.

177
00:11:55,282 --> 00:11:57,517
I ran as fast as I could,

178
00:11:57,617 --> 00:12:01,822
followed the framework,
found the tunnels.

179
00:12:01,922 --> 00:12:04,992
So how far are
the cells once we get in?

180
00:12:05,092 --> 00:12:06,359
It's close.

181
00:12:06,459 --> 00:12:07,494
[taps table twice]

182
00:12:07,594 --> 00:12:09,396
Wouldn't bank on
those cells being full.

183
00:12:09,496 --> 00:12:10,697
After your disappearing act,

184
00:12:10,798 --> 00:12:12,499
he would've moved folks
off site.

185
00:12:12,599 --> 00:12:14,067
How do you know?

186
00:12:15,468 --> 00:12:17,070
It's what he would've done.

187
00:12:19,639 --> 00:12:21,374
He and the Croat
know each other.

188
00:12:21,474 --> 00:12:24,711
They go back. Way back.

189
00:12:24,812 --> 00:12:28,581
He knows how he thinks.

190
00:12:30,117 --> 00:12:31,518
Huh.

191
00:12:31,618 --> 00:12:32,719
So they buddies, then?

192
00:12:32,820 --> 00:12:37,390
Were. Took a shot at him.
Blew his ear off.

193
00:12:37,490 --> 00:12:41,361
He can bait him.
Lure him out of the arena.

194
00:12:41,461 --> 00:12:45,032
And we get him to tell me
where my son is.

195
00:12:45,132 --> 00:12:47,600
And we kill him.

196
00:12:47,700 --> 00:12:49,402
The rest of us
will get a jump on his people

197
00:12:49,502 --> 00:12:51,004
so he can't follow you.

198
00:12:51,104 --> 00:12:52,105
[Luther] I'm sorry.

199
00:12:52,205 --> 00:12:54,607
You said he shot
his ear off, right?

200
00:12:54,707 --> 00:12:56,043
So how is he gonna bait him?

201
00:12:56,143 --> 00:12:58,411
You don't think
he's gonna want payback?

202
00:12:58,511 --> 00:13:01,581
Eye for an eye?
Dick for an ear?

203
00:13:01,681 --> 00:13:04,117
And what if you're wrong?

204
00:13:04,217 --> 00:13:05,252
What if it doesn't work?

205
00:13:05,352 --> 00:13:06,419
It will work.

206
00:13:06,519 --> 00:13:09,222
Y'all gonna get us killed.
And for what?

207
00:13:09,322 --> 00:13:11,091
For my son.

208
00:13:11,191 --> 00:13:12,425
So that I can get my son.

209
00:13:12,525 --> 00:13:15,395
Your son is already dead!

210
00:13:15,495 --> 00:13:16,930
I think you know that.

211
00:13:17,030 --> 00:13:18,798
[Negan] All right,
you know what?

212
00:13:18,899 --> 00:13:22,502
It's been a long day.
Let's take five.

213
00:13:23,703 --> 00:13:25,906
[indistinct chatter]

214
00:13:37,184 --> 00:13:42,923
[loud whirring]

215
00:13:43,023 --> 00:13:46,259
[keys jangling]
[door unlocking]

216
00:13:49,729 --> 00:13:51,498
[door shuts]

217
00:14:06,713 --> 00:14:12,785
[soothing Croatian choir music,
Proplakat Ce Zora , plays]

218
00:14:12,886 --> 00:14:14,354
[door opens]

219
00:14:18,425 --> 00:14:19,859
[door shuts]

220
00:14:21,094 --> 00:14:22,629
[sighs]

221
00:14:24,764 --> 00:14:26,366
Chilly in here,
isn't it?

222
00:14:30,770 --> 00:14:31,838
[switches on heat]

223
00:14:31,939 --> 00:14:34,707
[The Croat] There we are!

224
00:14:36,409 --> 00:14:39,346
Not bad for a jail, no?

225
00:14:39,446 --> 00:14:41,081
[chuckles]

226
00:14:47,454 --> 00:14:49,589
Nicer than yours, I imagine.

227
00:14:50,590 --> 00:14:51,992
Lights.

228
00:14:52,092 --> 00:14:54,527
Heat, music.

229
00:14:54,627 --> 00:14:55,695
Drink.

230
00:14:55,795 --> 00:14:57,664
Food.

231
00:15:01,834 --> 00:15:03,770
You must be hungry.

232
00:15:06,806 --> 00:15:08,608
Pasticada.

233
00:15:14,982 --> 00:15:17,517
It isn't magic, I promise.

234
00:15:19,953 --> 00:15:22,722
Only science.

235
00:15:22,822 --> 00:15:26,893
That was my profession.
Alternative energy.

236
00:15:26,994 --> 00:15:31,398
So naturally,
when I first arrived here,

237
00:15:31,498 --> 00:15:33,100
I couldn't
help asking myself,

238
00:15:33,200 --> 00:15:37,570
what is the most abundant
natural resource

239
00:15:37,670 --> 00:15:39,139
on this island?

240
00:15:42,309 --> 00:15:43,543
Death.

241
00:15:43,643 --> 00:15:45,245
The sewers are full of it.

242
00:15:45,345 --> 00:15:47,580
As the bodies break down,
they produce methane,

243
00:15:47,680 --> 00:15:50,783
and because the intermolecular
forces are weak,

244
00:15:50,883 --> 00:15:56,223
the gas can be pressurized
into a liquid fuel

245
00:15:56,323 --> 00:15:58,891
at regular temperatures.

246
00:16:00,327 --> 00:16:02,329
Amazing, isn't it?

247
00:16:03,896 --> 00:16:09,302
What we have built here
is a sanctuary.

248
00:16:15,242 --> 00:16:17,410
And all are welcome.

249
00:16:23,050 --> 00:16:26,553
So, why are you here,

250
00:16:26,653 --> 00:16:29,189
and whom did you bring with you?

251
00:16:31,058 --> 00:16:32,759
[sighs]

252
00:16:34,661 --> 00:16:35,928
[silverware clanking]

253
00:16:36,029 --> 00:16:40,467
You understand,
I can't offer you refuge

254
00:16:40,567 --> 00:16:42,535
until you no longer
pose a threat.

255
00:16:44,904 --> 00:16:46,639
Because above all, above all

256
00:16:46,739 --> 00:16:50,310
in this vicious, monstrous
world,

257
00:16:50,410 --> 00:16:53,513
we must stay safe.

258
00:16:57,950 --> 00:17:03,490
[record crackles, skips]

259
00:17:03,590 --> 00:17:05,525
You inspected the meat?

260
00:17:08,194 --> 00:17:13,133
Rotten meat can host
all type of bacteria.

261
00:17:13,233 --> 00:17:16,002
And without the treatment
that we once had,

262
00:17:16,103 --> 00:17:18,137
all potentially deadly.

263
00:17:21,441 --> 00:17:25,512
Why would you serve me
rotten meat?

264
00:17:25,612 --> 00:17:27,646
-Actually, it was--
-Ah, ah!

265
00:17:27,747 --> 00:17:33,753
[tense, sinister music]

266
00:17:51,671 --> 00:17:53,106
Ahh.

267
00:17:54,006 --> 00:17:55,508
Ahh?

268
00:18:02,482 --> 00:18:04,784
[gulps]

269
00:18:10,657 --> 00:18:12,259
[crack]

270
00:18:18,831 --> 00:18:22,101
[pants]

271
00:18:28,875 --> 00:18:33,880
[tense, sinister music]

272
00:18:33,980 --> 00:18:35,148
[door opens]

273
00:18:39,152 --> 00:18:42,822
[walkers growling]

274
00:18:59,572 --> 00:19:05,678
[dark, wistful music]

275
00:19:39,612 --> 00:19:41,180
[Negan coughs]

276
00:19:42,249 --> 00:19:44,851
Hey, sorry. I, um...

277
00:19:51,424 --> 00:19:53,660
I found this in the back of
one of those tourist shops.

278
00:19:53,760 --> 00:19:56,496
I remember, uh...

279
00:19:56,596 --> 00:19:59,599
I remember Hershel used to
wear one sort of like it.

280
00:19:59,699 --> 00:20:02,068
Thought maybe you could give
it to him when you see him.

281
00:20:04,771 --> 00:20:07,974
He's wrong, Luther.
He is wrong.

282
00:20:08,074 --> 00:20:09,842
Your plan is gonna work.

283
00:20:09,942 --> 00:20:12,545
If you wanna talk about it
or whatever, I...

284
00:20:13,246 --> 00:20:18,451
Contrary to popular belief,
I do occasionally...

285
00:20:18,551 --> 00:20:20,420
know how to shut up.

286
00:20:35,134 --> 00:20:37,236
[chairs creaks]

287
00:20:39,806 --> 00:20:42,775
When the Croat
showed up at our gates...

288
00:20:44,744 --> 00:20:48,748
I told Hershel...
to get in the root cellar.

289
00:20:51,518 --> 00:20:53,486
I tried to make him hide.

290
00:20:53,586 --> 00:20:55,221
By then, I could've said left
and he'd go right

291
00:20:55,322 --> 00:20:57,324
just to spite me.

292
00:20:57,424 --> 00:20:58,891
And he went and grabbed
his shovel and a brick

293
00:20:58,991 --> 00:21:01,193
like that was gonna do anything.

294
00:21:03,162 --> 00:21:05,131
And I told him he was stupid.

295
00:21:06,999 --> 00:21:09,369
He told me to get off
his damn back for once.

296
00:21:14,507 --> 00:21:16,876
And that is the last thing
that we said to each other.

297
00:21:17,777 --> 00:21:21,548
And I screwed up
so many ways before then.

298
00:21:21,648 --> 00:21:24,451
Fumbling through,
doing it by ourself...

299
00:21:29,188 --> 00:21:30,390
There weren't a lot of people

300
00:21:30,490 --> 00:21:34,293
that meant anything
to me in this world.

301
00:21:34,394 --> 00:21:38,431
But there were enough.

302
00:21:38,531 --> 00:21:42,134
And whatever's left of all
of them is inside this box.

303
00:21:45,037 --> 00:21:47,006
And I'm...

304
00:21:51,911 --> 00:21:53,913
A few years ago,

305
00:21:54,013 --> 00:21:55,448
Joshua, Annie, and I,

306
00:21:55,548 --> 00:21:58,585
we were living in this little
cabin outside of New Babylon.

307
00:22:00,219 --> 00:22:01,788
One day, Annie decided
to go into town

308
00:22:01,888 --> 00:22:03,690
to do some trading.

309
00:22:06,225 --> 00:22:09,228
When she wasn't home
at nightfall, I, uh...

310
00:22:09,328 --> 00:22:12,331
I knew something had gone wrong.

311
00:22:12,432 --> 00:22:16,636
I went looking for her.
I found her.

312
00:22:16,736 --> 00:22:18,705
And she had been...

313
00:22:21,073 --> 00:22:22,274
[sighs]

314
00:22:22,375 --> 00:22:23,510
She had been--

315
00:22:23,610 --> 00:22:27,714
She had been robbed,
beaten, and, um...

316
00:22:30,116 --> 00:22:33,820
She begged me not to
do something stupid.

317
00:22:33,920 --> 00:22:37,390
The hell, you know me.
I found 'em.

318
00:22:38,625 --> 00:22:40,960
All five of 'em.

319
00:22:41,060 --> 00:22:43,896
Some shit drinking hole.

320
00:22:45,765 --> 00:22:49,001
Honestly, I don't think I
even wanted to kill 'em.

321
00:22:49,101 --> 00:22:53,005
After that, we were on the run,
and it was very hard for Annie.

322
00:22:53,105 --> 00:22:54,841
So I put 'em on a wagon train
to Missouri,

323
00:22:54,941 --> 00:22:57,143
and I said I'd be
right behind 'em.

324
00:22:59,245 --> 00:23:01,213
I stayed.

325
00:23:01,313 --> 00:23:04,350
I think about them
every single day.

326
00:23:04,451 --> 00:23:06,352
I hope to god they are okay,

327
00:23:06,453 --> 00:23:09,255
and maybe I have no right
in hoping that.

328
00:23:11,157 --> 00:23:12,992
I don't know, Maggie.

329
00:23:14,827 --> 00:23:17,697
I mean, what else do we have?

330
00:23:17,797 --> 00:23:19,265
Besides hope.

331
00:23:23,503 --> 00:23:25,705
[Negan sighs]

332
00:23:25,805 --> 00:23:27,607
I thought you knew
how to shut up.

333
00:23:36,983 --> 00:23:42,054
[walkers growling]

334
00:23:42,154 --> 00:23:45,892
[tense music]

335
00:23:45,992 --> 00:23:51,363
[walker growling]

336
00:23:59,606 --> 00:24:01,207
[Negan] We can't
keep doing this.

337
00:24:01,307 --> 00:24:06,779
Been lookin' for this
friggin' dinosaur all day.

338
00:24:06,879 --> 00:24:11,618
[sighs] I've gotta find
a better place for you.

339
00:24:11,718 --> 00:24:15,254
And you have to speak.

340
00:24:15,354 --> 00:24:17,924
You know, I call out
for you, then you...

341
00:24:18,024 --> 00:24:19,692
you call back, all right?

342
00:24:19,792 --> 00:24:22,862
You're in trouble, you say so.

343
00:24:22,962 --> 00:24:26,733
Hey! Are you listening to me?

344
00:24:26,833 --> 00:24:30,102
No, Ginny,
you don't get to say no.

345
00:24:30,202 --> 00:24:31,904
All right, maybe back in the day

346
00:24:32,004 --> 00:24:33,806
you could go see
some state doctor

347
00:24:33,906 --> 00:24:36,275
and he would help you get
through all the horrible shit

348
00:24:36,375 --> 00:24:38,410
you've been through.

349
00:24:38,511 --> 00:24:40,479
But that is not
the case anymore,

350
00:24:40,580 --> 00:24:42,448
so you gotta skip
all the coping shit

351
00:24:42,549 --> 00:24:46,986
and get straight to
the staying alive shit.

352
00:24:47,086 --> 00:24:50,757
You hear me?

353
00:24:50,857 --> 00:24:52,525
Do you hear me!?

354
00:24:56,896 --> 00:24:58,631
[sighs]

355
00:24:58,731 --> 00:25:04,336
[birds chirping]

356
00:25:12,278 --> 00:25:13,780
Hey.

357
00:25:16,749 --> 00:25:18,918
You know what the problem is?

358
00:25:19,018 --> 00:25:20,987
The problem is
we don't have any leads.

359
00:25:21,087 --> 00:25:24,991
Or hell, maybe the
leads are all around us

360
00:25:25,091 --> 00:25:27,359
and we can't just see 'em.

361
00:25:28,260 --> 00:25:32,164
[walker growling]

362
00:25:32,264 --> 00:25:38,037
[unsettling music]

363
00:26:12,639 --> 00:26:15,341
[waves lapping]

364
00:26:19,178 --> 00:26:25,618
[tense, creaky music]

365
00:26:55,214 --> 00:26:59,218
[clinking]

366
00:27:11,497 --> 00:27:17,569
[hums gently, reverently]

367
00:27:20,639 --> 00:27:23,142
[chanting]
Doma smo! Doma smo!

368
00:27:23,242 --> 00:27:27,046
Doma smo! Doma smo!

369
00:27:27,146 --> 00:27:32,985
[humming continues]

370
00:27:34,186 --> 00:27:37,656
[All] Doma smo! Doma smo!

371
00:27:37,757 --> 00:27:39,759
Doma smo! Doma smo!

372
00:27:39,859 --> 00:27:41,761
We are home!

373
00:27:41,861 --> 00:27:47,133
[crowd cheering]

374
00:27:47,233 --> 00:27:51,971
[all hum]

375
00:27:52,071 --> 00:27:54,040
[The Croat] We are family.

376
00:27:55,241 --> 00:27:56,375
Tonight...

377
00:27:57,409 --> 00:27:59,311
Tonight...

378
00:27:59,411 --> 00:28:02,815
we celebrate
our fallen brother.

379
00:28:02,915 --> 00:28:06,452
Not mourn, no.

380
00:28:06,552 --> 00:28:09,822
Because death is no end.

381
00:28:09,922 --> 00:28:12,992
It is our fuel.

382
00:28:13,092 --> 00:28:18,497
Because people
are a resource!

383
00:28:18,597 --> 00:28:21,600
[crowd cheering]

384
00:28:21,700 --> 00:28:27,807
[humming continues]

385
00:28:45,157 --> 00:28:50,229
[humming ends]

386
00:29:03,509 --> 00:29:09,448
[crowd cheering]

387
00:29:10,817 --> 00:29:13,452
[cheering dies down]

388
00:29:15,487 --> 00:29:18,457
[methane escaping from mask]

389
00:29:19,125 --> 00:29:21,593
Anything to say?

390
00:29:23,029 --> 00:29:25,031
Last chance, my friend.

391
00:29:26,198 --> 00:29:27,967
[crowd shouting]

392
00:29:30,336 --> 00:29:36,308
[crowd cheering, laughing]

393
00:29:41,513 --> 00:29:43,983
[clanking]

394
00:29:45,517 --> 00:29:50,289
[panting]

395
00:29:56,028 --> 00:30:01,000
[The Croat] [speech warped]
Let's begin!

396
00:30:02,134 --> 00:30:04,803
[coughs]

397
00:30:11,377 --> 00:30:15,481
[walker growling]

398
00:30:18,550 --> 00:30:23,189
[crowd cheering, laughing]

399
00:30:28,594 --> 00:30:32,031
[music intensifies]
[walker growling]

400
00:30:44,343 --> 00:30:48,614
[walker growling]

401
00:30:49,916 --> 00:30:54,353
[crowd disappointed, groaning]

402
00:30:57,856 --> 00:30:59,458
[grunts]

403
00:30:59,558 --> 00:31:01,793
[crowd groaning]

404
00:31:03,429 --> 00:31:07,699
[glass shattering]

405
00:31:09,735 --> 00:31:13,305
[crowd shouting]

406
00:31:14,540 --> 00:31:20,579
[tense, pulsating music]

407
00:31:33,259 --> 00:31:36,228
[crowd shouting]

408
00:31:44,436 --> 00:31:45,871
[cage rattles]

409
00:31:45,972 --> 00:31:51,343
[walker growling]

410
00:31:53,980 --> 00:31:59,185
[music continues]

411
00:32:01,653 --> 00:32:06,458
[walkers growling]

412
00:32:13,832 --> 00:32:15,301
[grunts]

413
00:32:16,335 --> 00:32:18,971
[walkers growling]

414
00:32:20,806 --> 00:32:23,642
[grunts]

415
00:32:26,378 --> 00:32:28,547
[crowd shouting]

416
00:32:35,221 --> 00:32:37,823
[crickets chirping]

417
00:32:45,497 --> 00:32:46,999
Here we go, right?

418
00:32:47,866 --> 00:32:49,568
I gotta say,

419
00:32:49,668 --> 00:32:51,070
I'm shitting more bricks

420
00:32:51,170 --> 00:32:53,505
than what's left in
the city right now.

421
00:32:55,874 --> 00:32:57,809
I don't know how you do it.

422
00:32:57,909 --> 00:33:00,412
Keep it together,
with your kid and all.

423
00:33:04,050 --> 00:33:09,688
Amaia, she says having a kid
in the city wouldn't be safe.

424
00:33:11,257 --> 00:33:13,092
Yeah, I don't know, I just...

425
00:33:14,893 --> 00:33:16,862
Yeah, she's probably right,
you know?

426
00:33:19,031 --> 00:33:20,832
Yeah, she's right.

427
00:33:22,434 --> 00:33:24,503
It isn't safe.

428
00:33:28,407 --> 00:33:30,542
So you have to
make it safe somehow.

429
00:33:33,445 --> 00:33:35,681
You do whatever it takes.

430
00:33:36,115 --> 00:33:38,317
[Amaia] Tommaso!

431
00:33:38,417 --> 00:33:39,618
Look who's here.

432
00:33:39,718 --> 00:33:41,520
[laughing]
Oh, shit!

433
00:33:43,622 --> 00:33:45,157
-Where you been?
-Ah!

434
00:33:45,257 --> 00:33:46,158
Inwood?

435
00:33:46,258 --> 00:33:49,461
-Aw, shh.
-[chuckles]

436
00:33:49,561 --> 00:33:50,962
Scrounge up anything good?

437
00:33:51,063 --> 00:33:52,531
Always good.

438
00:33:52,631 --> 00:33:54,966
[chuckling]

439
00:33:55,067 --> 00:33:56,968
Um...

440
00:34:05,544 --> 00:34:07,379
[Maggie]
Where'd you get that?

441
00:34:08,414 --> 00:34:09,848
Street.

442
00:34:09,947 --> 00:34:11,483
When?

443
00:34:13,219 --> 00:34:15,754
I know a little girl who likes
stuff like that, that's all.

444
00:34:20,458 --> 00:34:22,094
Take it.

445
00:34:26,931 --> 00:34:31,570
[loud whirring]
[walkers growling]

446
00:34:34,639 --> 00:34:39,678
That was the best show
this place has seen in years.

447
00:34:42,148 --> 00:34:46,952
I don't enjoy such barbarism,
but it had to be done.

448
00:34:49,987 --> 00:34:55,761
When the world became unstable,

449
00:34:55,860 --> 00:34:59,765
my family and I found
shelter in a post office.

450
00:34:59,865 --> 00:35:03,869
We were starving,
so I went to look for food.

451
00:35:03,969 --> 00:35:09,275
When I got back,
I smelled it immediately.

452
00:35:09,375 --> 00:35:11,910
My family.

453
00:35:12,010 --> 00:35:15,714
My wife, Mia,

454
00:35:15,814 --> 00:35:17,749
and my daughters Nika and Hana,

455
00:35:17,849 --> 00:35:21,920
and my son, Filip,

456
00:35:22,020 --> 00:35:24,923
had become a meal

457
00:35:25,023 --> 00:35:27,493
for another starving family.

458
00:35:29,161 --> 00:35:32,097
I was too distraught to
even think of killing myself,

459
00:35:32,198 --> 00:35:36,067
and by the time that
would've occurred to me,

460
00:35:36,168 --> 00:35:41,940
I had already found the man
who would become my new family

461
00:35:42,040 --> 00:35:46,445
and teach me how to protect
the things that matter,

462
00:35:46,545 --> 00:35:51,583
which makes me wonder
what it is you are protecting

463
00:35:51,683 --> 00:35:53,084
in that boot.

464
00:35:53,185 --> 00:35:56,522
[Armstrong struggles]

465
00:36:00,426 --> 00:36:01,627
Ooh.

466
00:36:01,727 --> 00:36:05,464
[Armstrong pants]

467
00:36:05,564 --> 00:36:07,366
[grunts]

468
00:36:13,739 --> 00:36:15,073
"Pearlie,

469
00:36:15,173 --> 00:36:19,478
"I don't know if
you'll even read this.

470
00:36:19,578 --> 00:36:23,815
"I feel dumb it took me
so long to realize

471
00:36:23,915 --> 00:36:26,785
"you all changed your numbers.

472
00:36:26,885 --> 00:36:29,688
"I wonder what those
other people thought

473
00:36:29,788 --> 00:36:33,859
"when they heard my messages.

474
00:36:33,959 --> 00:36:37,162
"I've been trying so damn hard,

475
00:36:37,263 --> 00:36:40,165
"but it's too much for me.

476
00:36:40,266 --> 00:36:44,503
"I'm too weak, and I
can't do it by myself.

477
00:36:44,603 --> 00:36:47,005
"I need help.

478
00:36:47,105 --> 00:36:49,140
"Please help me.

479
00:36:49,241 --> 00:36:52,378
"Please come find me.

480
00:36:52,478 --> 00:36:54,880
"I don't like it where I am,

481
00:36:54,980 --> 00:36:57,182
and I just want to come home--"

482
00:36:57,283 --> 00:36:58,917
Stop it!

483
00:37:03,422 --> 00:37:06,325
It's just me.

484
00:37:06,425 --> 00:37:09,461
No one else.

485
00:37:09,561 --> 00:37:11,597
I had two partners,
but they're dead.

486
00:37:14,600 --> 00:37:16,702
We came to bring
a wanted man home.

487
00:37:16,802 --> 00:37:20,572
Who is worth following here?

488
00:37:22,308 --> 00:37:24,676
His name is Negan.

489
00:37:31,817 --> 00:37:35,787
[clanking]

490
00:37:46,332 --> 00:37:48,634
[chuckles]

491
00:37:51,537 --> 00:37:54,340
Oh dang, for a big guy,
you are quiet.

492
00:37:54,440 --> 00:37:56,608
I just, you know,
seeing if there's any weapons

493
00:37:56,708 --> 00:37:58,477
I could pick up for tomorrow.

494
00:38:01,112 --> 00:38:03,014
Look,

495
00:38:03,114 --> 00:38:06,385
I know you're not the
president of my fan club.

496
00:38:06,485 --> 00:38:08,253
I get it, but all
you need to know is that

497
00:38:08,354 --> 00:38:10,589
we are on the same side
and this plan is gonna work.

498
00:38:10,689 --> 00:38:14,259
The two of you are
leaving here tonight.

499
00:38:14,360 --> 00:38:17,228
I think you got the
wrong idea about me.

500
00:38:17,329 --> 00:38:19,164
Do I?

501
00:38:23,535 --> 00:38:26,171
So this isn't you right here?

502
00:38:27,506 --> 00:38:29,541
Says that "if you have
any information on this man,

503
00:38:29,641 --> 00:38:32,644
"notify any office of
the New Babylon Marshals.

504
00:38:32,744 --> 00:38:34,680
Do not approach unless armed."

505
00:38:35,747 --> 00:38:36,915
Mm.

506
00:38:37,015 --> 00:38:38,283
Where, uh,
where'd you get that?

507
00:38:38,384 --> 00:38:40,085
I got it from you.

508
00:38:40,185 --> 00:38:42,187
Must've been proud of yourself
to keep it on you.

509
00:38:44,089 --> 00:38:47,225
"Antisocial, prone
to extreme violence,

510
00:38:47,325 --> 00:38:50,662
"with above-average
intelligence and charisma.

511
00:38:50,762 --> 00:38:52,431
Do not trust him."

512
00:38:55,567 --> 00:38:58,470
The thing is...

513
00:38:58,570 --> 00:39:02,140
that I have people
depending on me, Luther.

514
00:39:02,240 --> 00:39:04,810
So respectfully?

515
00:39:04,910 --> 00:39:06,144
No.

516
00:39:06,244 --> 00:39:09,347
I ain't goin' anywhere.

517
00:39:10,549 --> 00:39:12,684
Respectfully,

518
00:39:12,784 --> 00:39:15,286
people are depending
on me as well.

519
00:39:15,387 --> 00:39:17,889
So, you know.

520
00:39:18,957 --> 00:39:25,030
[tense music]

521
00:39:26,432 --> 00:39:29,535
[chuckles]

522
00:39:29,635 --> 00:39:30,536
All right, here's the deal.

523
00:39:30,636 --> 00:39:32,671
I am, uh...

524
00:39:32,771 --> 00:39:35,373
I'ma try this one more time.

525
00:39:35,474 --> 00:39:36,842
All right, Luther?

526
00:39:36,942 --> 00:39:38,877
And I really hope this
doesn't turn into something

527
00:39:38,977 --> 00:39:41,079
it doesn't need to.

528
00:39:51,957 --> 00:39:53,759
Okay.

529
00:39:54,593 --> 00:39:57,362
[music intensifies]
[grunting]

530
00:39:57,463 --> 00:39:59,431
[yells]

531
00:40:01,800 --> 00:40:04,770
[grunts]

532
00:40:11,009 --> 00:40:13,879
[sputtering]

533
00:40:13,979 --> 00:40:15,947
[clank]

534
00:40:23,088 --> 00:40:29,127
[grunts]

535
00:40:31,463 --> 00:40:38,470
[tense music]

536
00:40:48,379 --> 00:40:54,486
[crickets chirping]

537
00:40:56,888 --> 00:41:02,961
[tense music]

538
00:41:17,308 --> 00:41:18,610
You didn't, by chance,

539
00:41:18,710 --> 00:41:20,679
check your bag before we left
this morning, did you?

540
00:41:25,984 --> 00:41:28,620
Maybe you didn't drop it all.
Maybe that asswipe stole him

541
00:41:28,720 --> 00:41:31,422
before you even had
a chance to drop him.

542
00:41:31,523 --> 00:41:37,362
[insects buzzing]

543
00:41:47,539 --> 00:41:49,775
[Negan] Oh shit, hold up.

544
00:41:49,875 --> 00:41:52,711
Oh, [grunts]

545
00:41:55,080 --> 00:41:57,215
All right, hold on to it for me.

546
00:41:58,516 --> 00:42:00,485
Good.

547
00:42:00,586 --> 00:42:04,656
Very gentle, go around.

548
00:42:04,756 --> 00:42:07,993
And... here you go, ma'am.

549
00:42:08,093 --> 00:42:10,696
the operation was
a complete success.

550
00:42:14,232 --> 00:42:16,668
All right.
Here's the thing, Ginny.

551
00:42:16,768 --> 00:42:20,171
I want you to listen, okay?

552
00:42:20,271 --> 00:42:22,874
[whistles two tones]

553
00:42:22,974 --> 00:42:26,712
That was the whistle that my
wife Lucille used, all right?

554
00:42:26,812 --> 00:42:28,847
She was sick and
couldn't get out of bed,

555
00:42:28,947 --> 00:42:30,181
and she would do that whistle.

556
00:42:30,281 --> 00:42:33,685
And it didn't matter what
I was doing or where I was.

557
00:42:33,785 --> 00:42:35,320
I came running.

558
00:42:36,287 --> 00:42:39,224
[whistles two tones]
Can you do that?

559
00:42:39,324 --> 00:42:40,525
[whistles two tones]

560
00:42:40,626 --> 00:42:41,960
[Negan] That was amazing.

561
00:42:42,060 --> 00:42:46,698
You do that and I'm not
around, I will be there.

562
00:42:46,798 --> 00:42:48,700
Deal?

563
00:42:48,800 --> 00:42:50,869
Talk is cheap anyway, kid.

564
00:42:50,969 --> 00:42:53,038
Believe me, I oughta know.

565
00:42:53,138 --> 00:42:54,940
It doesn't matter
what people say.

566
00:42:56,241 --> 00:43:00,679
[folksy guitar]

567
00:43:00,779 --> 00:43:04,582
* Hang me, oh, hang me

568
00:43:04,683 --> 00:43:07,085
* I'll be dead and gone

569
00:43:07,185 --> 00:43:08,720
It only matters what they do.

570
00:43:08,820 --> 00:43:12,423
* Hang me, oh, hang me

571
00:43:12,523 --> 00:43:16,561
* I'll be dead and gone

572
00:43:16,662 --> 00:43:19,898
* Wouldn't mind the hanging

573
00:43:19,998 --> 00:43:23,869
* But the laying in the
grave so long, poor boy *

574
00:43:23,969 --> 00:43:28,473
* I've been all
around this world *

575
00:43:30,608 --> 00:43:34,112
* Hang me, oh, hang me

576
00:43:34,212 --> 00:43:38,083
* I'll be dead and gone

577
00:43:38,183 --> 00:43:41,552
* Wouldn't mind the hanging

578
00:43:41,653 --> 00:43:45,724
* But the laying in the
grave so long, poor boy *

579
00:43:45,824 --> 00:43:50,328
* I've been all
around this world *

580
00:43:54,132 --> 00:43:57,202
Negan:
It's gonna work, Maggie.

581
00:43:57,302 --> 00:43:59,604
We're gonna get your boy back.

582
00:43:59,705 --> 00:44:04,109
Woman: You get your kid.
We kill the psycho.

583
00:44:04,209 --> 00:44:05,777
Don't screw it up.

584
00:44:05,877 --> 00:44:07,412
*

585
00:44:07,512 --> 00:44:08,446
[Woman screams]

586
00:44:08,546 --> 00:44:09,781
Hey, follow me!

587
00:44:09,881 --> 00:44:11,616
Negan?

588
00:44:11,717 --> 00:44:13,251
Fall in!

589
00:44:13,351 --> 00:44:15,286
*

590
00:44:15,386 --> 00:44:18,489
Nothing to be afraid of.
It's only me.

591
00:44:25,230 --> 00:44:27,933
Eli: Hi, I'm Eli Jorné,
EP showrunner of "Dead City,"

592
00:44:28,033 --> 00:44:32,403
and this is episode three,
"People are a Resource."

593
00:44:32,503 --> 00:44:35,841
*

594
00:44:35,941 --> 00:44:39,110
So, episode three has
this flashback storyline

595
00:44:39,210 --> 00:44:40,445
about Ginny and Negan,

596
00:44:40,545 --> 00:44:43,414
and we learn how
they formed their bond.

597
00:44:43,514 --> 00:44:47,252
Negan: You lost your Dino,
God damn it.

598
00:44:47,352 --> 00:44:52,090
*

599
00:44:52,190 --> 00:44:55,160
I think there's something
in Negan that wants to be there

600
00:44:55,260 --> 00:44:57,262
for people,
that can be there for people.

601
00:44:57,362 --> 00:44:58,964
[Whistles]

602
00:44:59,064 --> 00:45:00,431
Can you do that?

603
00:45:00,531 --> 00:45:02,000
[Whistles]

604
00:45:02,100 --> 00:45:03,802
That was amazing.

605
00:45:05,036 --> 00:45:07,472
The flashback is there
to help tell that story, too,

606
00:45:07,572 --> 00:45:09,640
about how Ginny
makes her way to the city.

607
00:45:09,741 --> 00:45:12,177
Well, she did it because
she's got Negan in her head.

608
00:45:12,277 --> 00:45:14,045
And so in that way,
we start to understand

609
00:45:14,145 --> 00:45:16,982
that it isn't just that he
helped her find a dinosaur doll,

610
00:45:17,082 --> 00:45:19,851
you know, he helped
her figure out how to live.

611
00:45:19,951 --> 00:45:21,853
*

612
00:45:21,953 --> 00:45:25,023
So in episode three,
we have yet another scene

613
00:45:25,123 --> 00:45:26,491
of Negan killing somebody.

614
00:45:26,591 --> 00:45:29,027
All you need to know
is that we are on the same side,

615
00:45:29,127 --> 00:45:30,528
and this plan is gonna --
The two of you

616
00:45:30,628 --> 00:45:33,231
are leaving here tonight.

617
00:45:33,331 --> 00:45:34,565
There's a lot
of implications there

618
00:45:34,665 --> 00:45:36,201
that Luther
intends to do to Negan

619
00:45:36,301 --> 00:45:38,169
what Negan ends up
doing to him.

620
00:45:38,269 --> 00:45:39,637
Everything that Luther is doing

621
00:45:39,737 --> 00:45:42,507
is coming from a place of love
for his people.

622
00:45:42,607 --> 00:45:44,742
And I think there's something
in Negan that even knows that.

623
00:45:44,843 --> 00:45:46,845
Okay.
[Clink]

624
00:45:46,945 --> 00:45:48,379
[Grunts]
[Pan clatters]

625
00:45:48,479 --> 00:45:51,016
We see that moment when Negan
holds down Luther's head,

626
00:45:51,116 --> 00:45:54,252
and there's a look in his face
like there's something in him

627
00:45:54,352 --> 00:45:56,354
that kind of gets unleashed
a little bit there,

628
00:45:56,454 --> 00:45:58,189
and he knows it
and maybe he fears it.

629
00:45:58,289 --> 00:45:59,657
And it's just
a small, little moment,

630
00:45:59,757 --> 00:46:01,359
but he looks down at his hand,

631
00:46:01,459 --> 00:46:03,528
and it's this wound
that got opened up.

632
00:46:03,628 --> 00:46:06,364
It's like these sort of
monstrous forces in him

633
00:46:06,464 --> 00:46:09,734
that seem to come out
whether he likes it or not.

634
00:46:09,835 --> 00:46:12,003
*

635
00:46:12,103 --> 00:46:15,340
The Croat and the Boratzi
are holed up in this big arena.

636
00:46:15,440 --> 00:46:17,508
That was really fun to build.

637
00:46:17,608 --> 00:46:19,210
The production designer,
Scott Murphy,

638
00:46:19,310 --> 00:46:21,179
just did
an incredible job there.

639
00:46:21,279 --> 00:46:22,447
There were these suites
all around,

640
00:46:22,547 --> 00:46:24,549
and those were our offices.

641
00:46:24,649 --> 00:46:26,517
So I'd be sitting there
doing rewrites,

642
00:46:26,617 --> 00:46:28,753
and I'd hear crazy stuff
happening down below --

643
00:46:28,854 --> 00:46:31,722
screaming and walkers
and groans and whatnot.

644
00:46:31,823 --> 00:46:33,358
The Croat: Here we are.

645
00:46:33,458 --> 00:46:36,427
*

646
00:46:36,527 --> 00:46:39,931
Not bad for a jail, no?
[Chuckles]

647
00:46:40,031 --> 00:46:41,933
The Croat never does anything
just to do it,

648
00:46:42,033 --> 00:46:43,101
just to be nice.

649
00:46:43,201 --> 00:46:44,535
There's always strategy there.

650
00:46:44,635 --> 00:46:46,905
And in this case,
he's trying to say to Armstrong,

651
00:46:47,005 --> 00:46:50,608
"If you give me what I want,
you can become a part of this."

652
00:46:50,708 --> 00:46:52,477
But I think Armstrong
knows on some level

653
00:46:52,577 --> 00:46:54,612
that's a dangerous game
to be playing.

654
00:46:54,712 --> 00:46:57,082
And so he withholds
the information,

655
00:46:57,182 --> 00:47:00,585
and of course, that leads
to a lot of trouble for him.

656
00:47:00,685 --> 00:47:04,755
[Crowd chanting indistinctly,
cheers]

657
00:47:04,856 --> 00:47:06,791
*

658
00:47:06,892 --> 00:47:08,927
Methane, you know,
if you breathe it in,

659
00:47:09,027 --> 00:47:13,598
it can really just kind of slow
everything down and mess you up.

660
00:47:13,698 --> 00:47:15,300
[Walker growls]

661
00:47:15,400 --> 00:47:16,968
There's this key moment --

662
00:47:17,068 --> 00:47:21,940
Armstrong realizes he could get
the key out of his stomach.

663
00:47:22,040 --> 00:47:23,674
And that's when I think we start
to realize

664
00:47:23,774 --> 00:47:26,577
this is weirdly a kind of test
or a challenge

665
00:47:26,677 --> 00:47:29,847
to see what Armstrong's made of.

666
00:47:29,948 --> 00:47:31,582
And then there's
this second key moment,

667
00:47:31,682 --> 00:47:34,619
which is when Armstrong
reaches to get his boot.

668
00:47:34,719 --> 00:47:35,954
And that's what
it was all about.

669
00:47:36,054 --> 00:47:37,622
The Croat has put him
in this situation

670
00:47:37,722 --> 00:47:40,425
where his life is on the line
and something slips out.

671
00:47:40,525 --> 00:47:43,494
The thing that's going to
crack him and break him.

672
00:47:43,594 --> 00:47:48,699
*

673
00:47:48,799 --> 00:47:51,169
Through the tribes people
and their experiences,

674
00:47:51,269 --> 00:47:54,505
their ways of grieving,
it's gonna start to kind of

675
00:47:54,605 --> 00:47:56,841
crack Maggie and Negan
open a bit.

676
00:47:56,942 --> 00:47:58,643
Maggie: There weren't
a lot of people

677
00:47:58,743 --> 00:48:01,446
that meant anything to me
in this world,

678
00:48:01,546 --> 00:48:03,448
but there were enough.

679
00:48:03,548 --> 00:48:05,150
*

680
00:48:05,250 --> 00:48:09,387
And whatever's left of
all of them is inside this box.

681
00:48:09,487 --> 00:48:11,489
And Negan, too,
is gonna have to open up

682
00:48:11,589 --> 00:48:13,524
and be vulnerable about
his pushing his family away

683
00:48:13,624 --> 00:48:14,825
to save them the trouble.

684
00:48:14,926 --> 00:48:16,227
Negan: After that,
we were on the run,

685
00:48:16,327 --> 00:48:18,863
and it was
very hard for Annie.

686
00:48:18,964 --> 00:48:20,865
So I put him on
a wagon train to Missouri,

687
00:48:20,966 --> 00:48:23,501
and I said I'd be
right behind him.

688
00:48:25,470 --> 00:48:26,504
I stayed.

689
00:48:26,604 --> 00:48:28,206
And when they start to do that,

690
00:48:28,306 --> 00:48:31,476
the funny thing that starts to
happen is they start to connect.

691
00:48:31,576 --> 00:48:32,743
You know, maybe on some level,

692
00:48:32,843 --> 00:48:34,379
they're both
starting to understand

693
00:48:34,479 --> 00:48:36,414
that the only way out of this
is through each other.

694
00:48:36,514 --> 00:48:38,183
I don't know, Maggie.

695
00:48:38,283 --> 00:48:40,018
*

696
00:48:40,118 --> 00:48:42,853
Hey, what else do we have

697
00:48:42,954 --> 00:48:44,489
besides hope?

698
00:48:44,589 --> 00:48:50,561
*

699
00:48:50,661 --> 00:49:02,140
[outro music]

